				<div class="x-element k-672ca257 w w-heading">
					<h2 class="x-heading-title x-size-default">The one beauty niche <span class="hl">that's genuinely a retail business too</span></h2>				</div>
		<div class="x-element k-77bc270d c-con-full c-flex c-con c-child">
		<div class="x-element k-3c57f4f c-con-full c-flex c-con c-child">
				<div class="x-element k-6bebe88e w w-text-editor">
									<p>Hair extension studios carry something almost no other beauty business does: real, expensive inventory. Premium Remy human hair in dozens of colours, lengths and textures sitting on shelves — which means the marketing has to sell trust in sourcing and colour-matching, not just styling skill.</p>								</div>
				<div class="x-element k-235ae926 w w-heading">
					<h3 class="x-heading-title x-size-default">Dubai's climate is a genuine, differentiating factor — not marketing fluff</h3>				</div>
				<div class="x-element k-2b6f66a0 w w-text-editor">
									<p>Tape-in adhesive that lasts 6-8 weeks in a temperate climate realistically lasts closer to 4-5 weeks for clients spending real time in Dubai&#8217;s heat and humidity. Studios that address this honestly — and recommend heat-resistant techniques like micro-link for the right clients — build far more trust than those that oversell a single method to everyone.</p>								</div>
				<div class="x-element k-7c7a5d76 w w-heading">
					<h3 class="x-heading-title x-size-default">The reorder cycle is the real business model</h3>				</div>
				<div class="x-element k-75e1ceb0 w w-text-editor">
									<p>Unlike most beauty services, extensions have a built-in, technique-specific reorder timeline. Marketing that reminds clients before their maintenance window — rather than waiting for them to notice their extensions slipping — is one of the highest-leverage retention plays in this entire industry.</p>								</div>
				</div>
